---
import EvidenceImage from './EvidenceImage.astro';
import {photo} from '../data/evidence';
import '../styles/shipping-checklist.css';
import ReadingHeader from './ReadingHeader.astro';
import PageContents from './PageContents.astro';
const topics=[
 ['Part protection','Mark cosmetic faces, sealing surfaces, threads, fragile edges, cleanliness and corrosion-protection needs. Specify pack weight or quantity limits and receiving-site handling requirements.','Agree protective materials, separation between parts and protection for threads and mating surfaces. Cartons or wooden cases depend on the part, quantity and transport route.'],
 ['Pack identification','Part number, drawing revision, quantity per pack, batch identification and required labels.','Confirm available label, lot-reference and inspection-document formats. Use the same part and revision references on the packing list and agreed quality records.'],
 ['Delivery basis','Full delivery address, receiving contact, required arrival date, requested trade term/version and named place.','Confirm who books transport and handles export/import clearance, insurance, duties, taxes and local delivery. EXW, FOB or DDP options are quoted for the applicable destination and service.'],
 ['Documents','The document list required by procurement, logistics or your destination-side import contact.','We provide protective packing, a packing list, commercial invoice and shipment information. Material, finishing and dimensional records are included when specified in the order. Confirm which documents are available and who prepares each.'],
 ['Schedule','Separate your required arrival date from the desired dispatch date.','Production takes 7–14 business days after drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing. Transit is estimated separately and is not included in production time.'],
];
const archive=['shipment-2022-order-packing','shipment-2022-prepared-load','shipping-example'];
const contents=topics.map((row,index)=>({id:'shipping-topic-'+(index+1),label:row[0]}));
---
<article class="sh-page reading-page">
 <ReadingHeader title="Shipping CNC parts internationally" description="Agree packing, documents and transport responsibilities alongside the machining work." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Resources',href:'/resources/'},{label:'Delivery planning'}]}/>
 <PageContents entries={contents}/>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-section sh-checklist reading-section" id="section-2" aria-labelledby="checklist-title"><h2 id="checklist-title">Five topics to confirm before a quotation</h2><div class="sh-checklist-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Topic</span><span>Information you provide</span><span>Confirm in the quotation</span></div><ol>{topics.map((row,index)=><li id={'shipping-topic-'+(index+1)}><div>{index===0&&<><span id="section-3" aria-hidden="true"/><span id="protection-title" aria-hidden="true"/></>}{index===2&&<span id="transport-title" aria-hidden="true"/>}{index===3&&<><span id="delivery-package" aria-hidden="true"/><span id="section-4" aria-hidden="true"/><span id="documents-title" aria-hidden="true"/></>}<h3>{row[0]}</h3></div><div><span class="sh-mobile-label">Information you provide</span><p>{row[1]}</p></div><div><span class="sh-mobile-label">Confirm in the quotation</span><p>{row[2]}</p>{index===2&&<p><strong>DDP is not an automatic inclusion.</strong></p>}</div></li>)}</ol></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-section reading-section"><details><summary>Transport options and import documents</summary><p>Courier, air or sea arrangements depend on shipment size and destination. DHL, FedEx or UPS can be discussed when selecting a courier.</p><p>Agree additional customs documents before production with your importing entity or freight forwarder. Requirements depend on the destination and transaction.</p></details></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-archive reading-section" aria-labelledby="archive-title"><h2 id="archive-title">LZZ packing archive</h2><figure><div class="sh-archive-grid">{archive.map(id=><a href={photo(id).src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={'View original photograph: '+photo(id).alt}><EvidenceImage id={id} sizes="(max-width:600px) 90vw, 30vw"/></a>)}</div><figcaption>LZZ packing archive · November 2022. Packing varies by part, quantity and route. These images do not establish a customer, destination, carrier, trade term or delivery outcome for a new order.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <nav class="sh-wrap sh-related reading-related" aria-label="Related resources"><div><h3>Related part examples</h3><p>Each custom part requires its own drawing and quote.</p><a class="sh-secondary" href="/products/small-batch-cnc-machining-manufacturer-complex-aluminum-housings/">Complex aluminum housings</a></div><div><h3>Learn more</h3><div class="sh-related-links"><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/how-we-work/">How We Work</a><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/rfq-checklist/">RFQ Checklist</a></div></div><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a></nav>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-rfq sh-section reading-closing" id="section-5" aria-labelledby="rfq-title"><div><h2 id="rfq-title">Include delivery in your RFQ</h2><p>Send the controlled drawing, material and finish specification, and quantity alongside the five delivery topics above. Ask the quotation to identify any exclusions.</p></div><div class="sh-rfq-action"><a class="sh-button" href="/quote/">Prepare RFQ email</a><p>Review your draft before sending it from your email app.</p><a class="sh-email" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com">roger@lzz-cnc.com</a></div></section>
</article>
